{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat .pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md'","aggregated_output":"---\ntype: decision-log\nslug: adr-sealed-review-bundles-review\nowner: @pose-maintainers\nsensitivity: public-internal\ncreated_at: 2026-08-13\nlast_reviewed_at: 2026-08-13\nexpires_at: 2026-11-11\nsource_refs:\n  spec: \"pose-review-bundle-convergence\"\n  workflow: \"feature\"\n  commands: [\"pose lint-spec pose-review-bundle-convergence --ready-check\", \"pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp --report --report-task review-bundle-convergence\"]\n  external_sources: []\n---\n\n# decision-log: adr-sealed-review-bundles-review\n\n## Context\n\nThe current full-body review scope digest lets closeout bookkeeping alter the\nsubject that was just approved. Component-aware review also exposed transient\nprovider merge provenance and excessive full-plan rereview. The proposed ADR\nseparates a canonical sealed bundle from its attestation and makes POSE the\noffline verifier while an optional Conductor workflow owns orchestration.\n\n## Current state\n\nADR `2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations` is accepted. The core,\nCLI, read-only MCP, schemas, opt-in migration, scoped provenance bridge,\nEnglish/pt-BR distribution and fresh-repository convergence smoke are\nimplemented under `pose-review-bundle-convergence`.\n\n## Next checks\n\n- Prove `prepare -> validate -> seal -> review -> attest -> close` converges\n  without a second bundle or review.\n- Prove lifecycle, state, assessment, report and attestation mutations do not\n  change the sealed bundle.\n- Prove every governed semantic, source, policy and required-evidence mutation\n  supersedes the affected bundle.\n- Verify synthetic merge/squash subjects by patch and tree/content digests.\n- Verify policy-bounded targeted criterion reuse and complete final projection.\n- Verify a new delivery target cannot stale unrelated closed specs and that no\n  historical evidence must be regenerated to recover the strict gate.\n- Verify repeated mapping warnings and inactive completion tools are grouped in\n  human output while canonical JSON retains complete provenance.\n- Verify offline flow, installed-binary parity and schema-v1/v2 migration before\n  promoting the feature from preview.\n\n## Risks\n\nSemantic projection may omit a meaningful input or retain an operational input,\ncausing false freshness or false staleness. Keep unknown paths fail-closed,\nrequire include/exclude golden fixtures and review production deltas after the\nfirst opt-in release. Criterion reuse may miss cross-cutting effects; disable it\nfor high-criticality profiles until sliced-input evidence proves safe.\n\n## Next owner\n\n`@pose-maintainers`.\n\n## References\n\n- `spec:pose-review-bundle-convergence`\n- `adr:2026-08-13-sealed-review-bundles-and-attestations`\n- `adr:2026-08-12-component-aware-effective-review-plans`\n- `knowledge:pr15-component-aware-review-provenance`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"agent_message","text":"The earlier listed findings are fixed in their reviewed paths, including N37’s doctor binding. Two blockers remain: the adopted-policy child bypass with bundles disabled, and malformed or duplicate ADR metadata being treated as absence. Artifact-check and surface-check passed, as did the focused tests and `go vet`. The worktree remains unchanged."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_81","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nTwo medium blockers remain:\n\n- **N38:** An adopted policy with bundles disabled can report a receipt-closed milestone terminal after a member’s rejection, through the legacy `unreviewed_milestones` exception.\n- **N39:** Empty or duplicate ADR association metadata can become a known absence and grant a `when-justified` exemption.\n\nThe five prior findings are fixed in their reviewed paths. Artifact-check, surface-check, focused policy tests, round-ten regressions, and `go vet` passed. Custom probes could not run because the sandbox denied temporary-file creation. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\nApplied the review workflow and Go, security, documentation, delivery-evidence, and knowledge-governance rules. The JSON below contains every criterion, tool disposition, structural mapping, and finding.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N38\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go\",\n      \"line\": 2742,\n      \"summary\": \"Restrict the legacy declaredUnreviewed child exception to legacy closeout semantics. Schema 5 supports review_bundles=false. In that configuration, an aggregate's approved legacy attempt remains fresh when a child's review is subsequently rejected: ScopeDigest binds the child's content, not its verdict, and the legacy-attempt verification branch does not verify children. This condition then suppresses child-scope-open whenever unreviewed_milestones is present, even under adopted always. With an existing valid receipt, getCloseoutState can therefore return Terminal=true while its child is nonterminal. closedByReceipt propagates that result to reached, obligations, readiness and doctor. CLI repeated close independently checks the member gate and refuses, creating a disagreement between authoritative projections. Preserve child terminal failures under every adopted mode and cover an approved legacy-attempt milestone before and after member rejection, with bundles disabled and unreviewed_milestones present.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N39\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 89,\n      \"summary\": \"Preserve association-field presence and reject ambiguous or malformed declarations before proving absence. An explicit empty adrs: value is indistinguishable here from an absent field. parseInlineList also discards empty items, accepting adrs: [,] as an empty list. Duplicate adrs fields are overwritten by parseRoadmapFile, while duplicate ADR roadmaps fields are overwritten by SplitFrontmatter; for example adrs: [adr:decision.md] followed by adrs: [] silently removes the association. A roadmap with two canonical members and no other association consequently receives Known=true, Required=false under when-justified. This contradicts R3's technical contract that malformed or ambiguous association inputs cannot produce an exemption. Validate presence, list syntax and duplicate association keys in both directions, with negative regression fixtures.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N40\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/closeout_adr_associations.go\",\n      \"line\": 55,\n      \"summary\": \"The Markdown link extractor scans raw bodies, including fenced code, inline code and comments. An ADR containing a documented example such as a fenced [example](../roadmaps/example.md) is treated as a real reverse association input. If the illustrative roadmap does not exist, the inventory makes unrelated when-justified roadmap decisions unknown; if it exists, the example can spuriously require review. This over-enforces the gate rather than bypassing it, so it is accepted as a low residual risk.\",\n      \"action\": \"Exclude non-link Markdown contexts before extracting associations and add code-example and comment fixtures.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-12-13\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N41\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"disposition\": \"follow-up\",\n      \"file\": \".pose/adr/2026-11-03-governance-reads-use-bounded-operation-scoped-views.md\",\n      \"line\": 253,\n      \"summary\": \"git diff --check for the reviewed range exits 2 because the D10 amendment adds a blank line at EOF. This is a nonfunctional hygiene defect and is accepted as a low residual risk.\",\n      \"action\": \"Remove the extra blank line at EOF when addressing the review findings.\",\n      \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\",\n      \"review_by\": \"2026-11-20\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R8-N32\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:3556 now verifies exemption children and clears approval on a non-closed, unapproved or stale child; closeout_review_policy_test.go:1316 covers an exempt receipt-bearing milestone falling with its member. The focused TestCloseoutReviewPolicy run passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R9-N34\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:3518 evaluates adopted exemptions before the !policy.ReviewBundles return at 3576. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundTen/an_exempt_milestone_without_review_bundles_closes_by_its_receipt passed without skipping.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R9-N35\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/roadmaps.go:401 uses closedByReceipt for adopted predecessor warnings. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundTen/start_warnings_name_an_approved_but_unclosed_predecessor passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R9-N36\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:1823 propagates a failed inherited child's blockers instead of silently skipping it. TestCloseoutReviewPolicyRoundTen/a_roadmap's_own_approval_does_not_stand_over_a_fallen_exempt_milestone passed. N38 concerns the separate supported legacy-attempt and declaredUnreviewed closeout path.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R11-N37\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/doctor.go:1587 constructs cliGovernedStore(root), preserving the environment-bound resolver used by close. The CLI TestCloseoutReviewPolicy tests passed.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed R1-R7, the accepted cost-benefit ADR, D10 and its spec amendment, the specified implementation and governance paths, schemas, templates and distribution docs. Swept policy parsing/adoption/setup/update preservation; canonical and transferred members; forward/reverse ADR associations; protected baseline and mandatory-human handling; optional-review vetoes; receipt parsing, immutable publication, interrupted-close recovery and historical closure; CLI close, closeout-check, review-check, review verification and review-plan; reached/nextCloses; obligations, readiness and portfolio; roadmap gates; MCP closeout projection; federation; doctor; and the adversarial corpus. Ran context resolution, suggest-review, artifact-check, surface-check, focused domain/CLI/MCP policy tests, verbose round-ten regressions, go vet and diff hygiene. Artifact-check and surface-check exited 0; policy tests and vet passed. The attempted additional overlay probes failed before execution because no temporary directory was writable, so N38-N40 are established by the cited control flow rather than claimed custom runtime reproductions. Final git status was clean. No assessment, state refresh, index, repository edit or attestation was performed.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Distinguished executed checks and inspected control flow from implementer claims. Historical approvals require positive legacy evidence; unknown members fail exemption. D10's 492 MB measurement was not independently repeated because index/assessment writes are prohibited; it is documented decision evidence, while the 1 GiB constant and unchanged remaining bounds were verified in code. F5 remains explicitly documented scaling debt.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected guarded reevaluation, receipt ExpectAbsent publication, intent-before-status ordering and conflict handling. The change uses existing writer coordination and introduces no background lifecycle.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N38\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The supported bundles-disabled policy can produce conflicting terminal answers across closeout projections and CLI close.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N39\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Malformed and ambiguous association metadata is not consistently diagnosed before granting an exemption.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N38\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The remaining terminal-state exception propagates through consumers of closedByReceipt.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected decision reasons, canonical refs, unknown-input diagnostics, receipt corruption errors, doctor remediation and publication-conflict context. Diagnostics are bounded by the existing read and inventory limits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/install-and-upgrade-journeys-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Schema 5 deliberately rejects older engines, requires both enums and keeps references/transfer optional. Existing instances retain legacy semantics until explicit adoption; capability retirement preserves schema 5; historical plans retain their reading. Inspected the updated previous-release compatibility assertions and catalog/install paths.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N38\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A receipt-bearing aggregate can remain terminal over a rejected member in the supported legacy-attempt configuration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-9d28f40675908bcf\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The shared deterministic evaluator addresses review cost without removing explicit close. Receipts separate review exemption from lifecycle completion; schema 5 makes adoption explicit. D10 is a bounded capacity recalibration tied to observed corpus growth, with the structural scaling correction retained as F5.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-607ff681\",\n          \"basis\": \"R3\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The roadmap template exposes explicit adrs association metadata used by the deterministic roadmap predicate.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-7e629ade\",\n          \"basis\": \"R7\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The spec's artifact reconciliation explicitly includes D10 to restore operation on the current attributed-history corpus while retaining bounded reads.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-ec2d86f4\",\n          \"basis\": \"R1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The new accepted ADR records policy location, thresholds, defaults, historical compatibility and explicit close semantics.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared English, Portuguese and scaffold descriptions with runtime policy modes, receipt paths, adoption and exit-gate behavior. Templates expose adrs. N38 and N39 identify runtime departures from the documented contract; N41 records the nonfunctional amendment whitespace.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N40\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Literal Markdown examples can create spurious association failures; the bounded over-enforcement is retained as an owned low follow-up.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N39\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R3's malformed/ambiguous-input requirement is incomplete; N38 also violates the requirement to preserve member review standing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-9d28f40675908bcf\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The changes implement the policy, evaluator, receipts and required consumers within the amended spec. D10 and its tests/docs are explicitly reconciled artifacts. No new configuration command, MCP write tool or global ADR-reference grammar was added.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N38\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The local approval boundary must not suppress a member rejection under adopted semantics. Separately inspected receipt confinement, ADR regular-file checks, transfer resolution and immutable publication.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-9d28f40675908bcf\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A paired policy, one evaluator and an immutable terminal receipt are sufficient to separate review cost from closeout. Reusing adopt and existing writer guards avoids another settings service or lifecycle mechanism. Remote backlink inventory and broader ArtifactRef grammar remain excluded. D10 buys finite headroom; another budget refusal or unacceptable retained-memory cost invalidates that temporary choice and triggers F5's digest-only retention work. Inspected the adversarial corpus's parent-outlives-a-rejected-child case; N38 records its uncovered legacy-attempt variant.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed and exited 0. Output included artifact.claims=46, artifact.observed=157 and artifact.findings=920. The emitted broad orphan warnings did not fail the strict gate; the printed first recorded change set predates the current HEAD, and the implementation also collects the current attributed set.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-9d28f40675908bcf\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not run a state-writing assessment in the sealed checkout. Used sealed structure evidence and independently mapped all three supplied deltas.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Discovery writes assessment state and is prohibited by this review boundary. Component scope and applicable rules were checked from the brief, spec, matrix and suggest output.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not run the state-writing assessment. Inspected CLI/domain/MCP/federation boundaries and used sealed integration evidence plus the independently executed focused tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Did not run the state-writing assessment. Inspected changed code and the spec's explicit F1-F5 follow-ups; D10's retained-byte scaling debt remains documented as F5.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose context --task spec:pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --json\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only check requires the recorded review conclusion. This independent run must not record an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose context --task spec:pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --json\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only check is deferred until POSE records the verified run's conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully; selected security, documentation-style and backend-go rules and the review workflow.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose surface-check --spec pose-closeout-review-policy-by-cost-benefit --strict; exited 0 with surface.targets=1, surface.results=213 and surface.findings=0. Integration evidence: integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration. Production reachability evidence: reachability:pose-mcp/go/closeout-plan-reachability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Disposed from the sealed validation run as permitted for registered checks; did not rerun the state-writing validate producer. The bundle also seals build:pose-mcp/go/build and e2e:pose-mcp/go/multi-repo-agent-installed-journey. Independently ran the focused policy tests and go vet.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/closeout-review-policy-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used the sealed component validation evidence. Independently executed go test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli ./internal/mcpserver -run '^TestCloseoutReviewPolicy' -count=1, the verbose round-ten regression test and go vet ./...; all passed. Passing registered checks do not cover N38-N40.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
